  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Valuing Women&apos;s Work-Mapping of Informal Sector and its section with UCDW</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The grant is intended to support the mapping exercise in Zambia and Zimbabwe  which will be a critical step toward establishing a baseline and identifying key parameters of informal work - paid and underpaid and its intersection with care work, as well as its linkages to cross border trade within the Southern Africa (SAF) region. The mapping exercise will provide a basis for engaging key actors such as Governments, Private Sector, United Nation (UN) agencies and communities to dialogue, debate, research and develop policy interventions so that societies can truly value women&apos;s work, so that their contribution can be recognised, valued and measured and invested in as part of the regional economy.</narrative>
  </description>
